    <statement><p>Let <m>\vec F(x,y,z) = 5x^2\vec i - \sin(xz)(\vec i + \vec k)</m>.
Calculate the divergence:</p>
<p><m>\mbox{div }\vec F(x,y,z) =</m> <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2\cdot 5x-z\cos\mathopen{}\left(xz\right)-x\cos\mathopen{}\left(xz\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><me>\mbox{div } (5x^2\vec i - \sin(xz)(\vec i + \vec k)) = 10x-z\cos\mathopen{}\left(xz\right)-x\cos\mathopen{}\left(xz\right).</me>




</solution>
